creatures.haven-town.havC04.description:
{green|Deep One}

{gold|Special Ability : Water Warrior. Retaliated twice.}

On water terrain Deep Ones attack, defence and speed are increased by 1.

Retaliation refers to the counterattack of a stack that has been the target of a melee attack. All creatures have one retaliation per combat round with the exceptions of several creatures like Griffins, which have two retaliations per combat round. With the Counterstrike spell, it is possible for a hero to magically add one or two extra retaliations per combat round. For Deep Ones this means three or four in total.

creatures.haven-town.havC05.description:
{green|Arbalist}

{gold|Special Ability : Water Warrior. Shooter.}

On water terrain Arbalists attack, defence and speed are increased by 1.

Ranged attack is a special ability of creatures, which allows them to attack without engaging into hand-to-hand combat. Visually, typical ranged creature are armed with bows or crossbows (e.g. Elves or Archers), but there are also several creatures that use some kind of magic or elements (lightning, etc.), like Monks or Titans. However, this is only a visual effect and has no effect on the gameplay. When attacking in melee, most ranged creatures suffer melee penalty, which halves their damage. Ranged penalty halves the ranged damage farther away than 10 hexes.

creatures.haven-town.havC06.description:
{green|Elite Arbalist}

{gold|Special Ability : Water Warrior. Shooter. Enemy defence reduction 30%. Can cast Precise Marking spell.}

On water terrain Elite Arbalists attack, defence and speed are increased by 1.

Once per battle elite arbalists can cast Precise Marking spell - affected enemy stacks gain 50% more damege from shoots for three rounds. Effects of this spell can be countered by Air Shield (and vice versa).

