creatures.haven-town.havC07.description:
{green|Mermaid}

{gold|Special Ability : Water Warrior. Whirlpool Protector. Can cast Fortune. Always have +1 luck.}

On water terrain Mermaids attack, defence and speed are increased by 1.

When a hero enters the whirlpool, he loses 50% rounded up (i.e. is left with 50% rounded down) of the creatures in his army's weakest stack. The weakness is determined by the total Fight Value of the stacks. With Mermaids in army, a hero can enter whirlpools without losing creatures.

Mermaids can cast two times per battle Fortune spell at advanced level (spell duration - 6 rounds).

The positive luck ability of mermaids can be affected by Hourglass of the Evil Hour or Cursed Ground magical terrain only. Their luck cannot be decreased below +1 by any other luck modifier. Mermaids are unable to get luck unless being commanded by a hero, like all the other neutral creatures, despite the game saying that they have +1 luck.

creatures.haven-town.havC09.description:
{green|Marid}

{gold|Special Ability : Water Warrior. Flying. Immune to water damaging spells.}

On water terrain Marids attack, defence and speed are increased by 1.

Flying is a special ability of creatures, which allows them to bypass obstacles (e.g. walls) during combat. Having creatures with this special ability in a hero's army does not affect the movement of that hero on the adventure map in any way (meaning that flying creatures also cause a movement penalty on non-native terrain). Flying creatures are always immune to Quicksand.

Spell immunity is creature special ability which makes them unable to be target of the specific spell or a range of spells. The immunity also regards creature abilities which cause the same effect as the specific spell or spells (for example, Troglodytes are immune to the Blind spell as well as Unicorns' blinding special ability), even if technically this ability doesn't mean respective spell (for example, Gold and Black Dragons are immune to the Resurrection spell as well as Archangels' resurrecting special ability). The Orb of Vulnerability can bypass some spell immunities.

creatures.haven-town.havC10.description:
{green|Marid Sultan}

{gold|Special Ability : Water Warrior. Flying. Immune to water damaging spells. No enemy retaliation.}

On water terrain Sultan Marids attack, defence and speed are increased by 1.

Flying is a special ability of creatures, which allows them to bypass obstacles (e.g. walls) during combat. Having creatures with this special ability in a hero's army does not affect the movement of that hero on the adventure map in any way (meaning that flying creatures also cause a movement penalty on non-native terrain). Flying creatures are always immune to Quicksand.

